 " is the search."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"6e3c2fe3-0288-44e2-8382-3572ad307f86"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: a circle of the band ",
 StyleBox["W", "TI"],
 " around ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " is a shortest cycle of the subgraph induced on ",
 StyleBox["W", "TI"],
 " whose removal leaves ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " in a component that reaches no further than the band."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"64e05878-6345-46d7-b9ef-e3e5c8a03e2c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The point form takes the band at ",
 StyleBox["d(c, p)", "TI"],
 " and keeps the circles through ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 ". Option ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<RadiusDelta\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"deltaIn", ",", " ", "deltaOut"}], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "92f3505c-e76c-4339-b865-296644fb1994"],
 " widens it to ",
 StyleBox["d(c, p)", "TI"],
 " \[Minus] ",
 StyleBox["deltaIn", "TI"],
 " \[LessEqual] ",
 StyleBox["d(c, v)", "TI"],
 " \[LessEqual] ",
 StyleBox["d(c, p)", "TI"],
 " + ",
 StyleBox["deltaOut", "TI"],
 ". A scalar ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<RadiusDelta\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "delta"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ee248743-de05-45ee-ad99-6e5202dc5850"],
 " means ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "delta"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9c943edb-c3f7-4bec-b34f-37d322a703a5"],
 ", outward only. The default is ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10c41f65-874c-44f8-aa0f-a6b76a990cbb"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"cb085b82-2aa0-436b-89d3-2a60bd17176c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["A circle need not exist.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " On a lattice a single distance shell has no two adjacent vertices, so it \
spans no cycle and the family is empty. Widening the radius to a band fixes \
it."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"73759adf-4150-47c0-b842-915cb381751a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Its graph \[LongDash] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
     "WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["circle", "TI"], ",", " ", "\"\<Graph\>\""}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e8ecfe0-0b22-4939-9212-a76f455d6206"],
 " \[LongDash] is a ",
 Cell[BoxData["List"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e8f9664-4ef6-4b6f-8921-5f27c90cac35"],
 " of necklaces, cut from the band along a radial seam: a geodesic from ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " to just outside the band. A necklace is a DAG with one source ",
 StyleBox["s1", "TI"],
 " and one sink ",
 StyleBox["u", "TI"],
 ". It is the cycle family ",
 StyleBox["opened",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " at its closing arrow ",
 StyleBox["u", "TI"],
 " -> ",
 StyleBox["s1", "TI"],
 ", which is left out, so the DAG is acyclic."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"28552eff-75c8-4dc1-a031-e12ecf0651f2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A member is the open chain ",
 StyleBox["s1", "TI"],
 " \[Ellipsis] ",
 StyleBox["u", "TI"],
 ", read cyclically: a cyclic vertex list whose first vertex is not repeated. \
Its ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Length\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cb4c3ae9-795c-4a32-a3e3-942abf9ad7d6"],
 " counts the closing edge too, so a circle of ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " vertices has length ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4376af90-ff77-4f77-aded-e58d06b72aa6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every member separates. That the necklaces carry every circle exactly once \
needs two hypotheses on the substrate \[LongDash] the winding functional and \
the one-run hypothesis \[LongDash] which nothing here certifies. So ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Faithful\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "16c603fe-48ce-48b0-b654-b56516ff8453"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Undetermined"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry/ref/Undetermined", 
    "WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "7793ef13-d4a2-4c18-9fdb-76257d5565b7"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4e838ab2-8f65-452f-9882-4365f91d860b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Inside an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraScene"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry/ref/InfraScene", 
    "WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "219aec33-6ac5-4369-8e62-c5ba0fa2100a"],
 ", the token ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraCircle", "[", 
   RowBox[{"c", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d0b82ae7-4e78-4e62-93c7-34914bf7a2bd"],
 " still reads ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " as a radius, unlike the head, where a bare second argument is always a \
point. This is an open inconsistency."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0d5f05d8-79d6-4a3f-a1eb-de0a628dacad"]
}, Open  ]],

